TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"transient","diagnosis":"Aborted before the worker committed anything, so the ownership gate \"conflict-domains\" failed on an empty change set rather than on a boundary violation. Evidence: diff.head equals baseRev 71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa with an empty patch; the lane worktree is clean (git status --porcelain empty, docs/ still holds only the pre-existing GATE0.md, CONTINGENCY patch, and .gitkeep), so no partial or uncommitted task work exists to preserve. The recorded cause is adapter-side: result-schema-mismatch wrapping result-projection-timeout, where the configured finalMessage capture for adapter \"spec-build-driver\" was not projected within 10000 ms and exitEvidencePassed was false; stderr \"spec-build-driver: agent produced no commit relative to the prepared base\" is the downstream consequence of that lost session, not an independent implementation finding. Nothing in the record implicates the task definition: the goal writes only docs/MORNING.md and docs/ANNOUNCE.md, both inside the binding conflictDomains prefix [\"docs\"], the single acceptance criterion ledger-sections is satisfiable entirely within that prefix, and both dependencies host-tooling and bench-harness are already merged into the prepared base as commits b474021 and 71f2beb. There is no needs-authority envelope, no workerOutcomeClaim, no steering, and no prior diagnosis, so there is no substantive defect for attempt-2 steering to correct and no out-of-task authority or gate-contract change to propose. This is a harness or session fault that should consume the bounded machinery-retry budget: re-dispatch the same task revision sha256:4c0b640cab49ea7ac3b57b4e23f66c726b92fcce08e77d0f8816814181c3ba0a unchanged on the same lane so the driver can capture a final message and land a commit."}
